width":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"1","left":"0","isLinked":false},"border_color":"#B5B5B5","padding":{"unit":"px","top":"10","right":"0","bottom":"20","left":"0","isLinked":false}},"elements":[{"id":"ac56aa6","elType":"widget","settings":{"typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Jost","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":16,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"300","text_color":"#6B6A6B","link_color":"#6B6A6B","__dynamic__":[],"typography_line_height":{"unit":"em","size":1.5,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":12,"sizes":[]},"editor":"<p>Fashion jewelry is a versatile accessory that can elevate any outfit, making it a staple in many people's wardrobes.<br />Despite its affordability, proper care is essential to maintain its quality and appearance over time.</p><p><strong>DOS FOR FASHION JEWELRY CARE</strong></p><p><strong>A. Store Jewelry Properly</strong></p><p>1. Keep it Separated: Store each piece of jewelry separately to prevent scratching, tangling, or damage.<br />2. Use Jewelry Boxes or Pouches: Store jewelry in soft pouches or lined jewelry boxes to protect them from dust and moisture, which can tarnish or damage the pieces.</p><p><strong>B. Clean Jewelry Regularly</strong></p><p>3. Use a Soft Cloth: Clean jewelry regularly with a soft jewelry cloth to remove dirt and oils that can dull its appearance.<br />4. Avoid Harsh Chemicals: Do not use harsh chemicals or cleaners that can damage the metal or stones of the jewelry.</p><p><strong>C. Handle Jewelry With Care</strong></p><p>5. Put Jewelry on Last: Put on jewelry after applying makeup, lotions, or perfumes to avoid exposing it to chemicals that can tarnish or damage the pieces.<br />6. Avoid Tugging or Pulling: Handle jewelry gently to prevent bending or breaking delicate chains or clasps.</p><p><strong>D. Check and Maintain Regularly</strong></p><p>7. Inspect Clasps and Settings: Regularly check clasps, prongs, and settings for any loosening or damage and have them repaired by a professional if needed.</p><p><strong>DON’TS FOR FASHION JEWELRY CARE</strong></p><p><strong>A. Expose Jewelry to Harsh Conditions</strong></p><p>1. Avoid Water and Moisture: Remove jewelry before swimming, showering, or using beauty products, as exposure to water and moisture can cause tarnishing and damage.<br />2. Keep Away from Heat and Sunlight: Store jewelry away from direct sunlight and heat sources to prevent fading or warping of materials.</p><p><strong>B. Wear Jewelry Continuously</strong></p><p>3. Remove During Activities: Take off jewelry before engaging in activities such as exercising, cleaning, or cooking to prevent damage from sweat, chemicals, or impact.<br />4. Avoid Sleeping with Jewelry: Remove jewelry before sleeping to prevent tangling, bending, or breakage while tossing and turning.</p><p><strong>C. Use Incorrect Cleaning Methods</strong></p><p>5. Avoid Abrasives: Do not use abrasive materials or rough cloths to clean jewelry, as they can scratch or damage the surfaces.<br />6. Skip Ultrasonic Cleaners: Refrain from using ultrasonic cleaners on fashion jewelry, as they can be too harsh and cause damage to delicate pieces.</p><p><strong>D. Neglect Maintenance</strong></p><p>7. Don't Ignore Repairs: If you notice any damage or issues with your jewelry, address them promptly to prevent further damage or loss of stones.<br />8. Don't Skip Regular Care: Neglecting regular cleaning and maintenance can lead to the deterioration of your fashion jewelry over time.</p>"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"}],"isInner":true,"isLocked":true},{"id":"6ba7a0f","elType":"container","settings":{"_title":"item #1","content_width":"full","lqd_parallax_settings_trigger_start":"top bottom","lqd_parallax_settings_trigger_end":"bottom top","lqd_sticky_row_offset":"0px","border_border":"solid","border_width":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"1","left":"0","isLinked":false},"border_color":"#B5B5B5","padding":